CON-21: weight the summary averages by the routing step length

updateStatistics() added one sample per routing step to the node depth,
storage volume and outfall flow sums, and DefaultReportPlugin divided them
by the number of steps (or of flowing steps for an outfall), so under a
variable routing step the short steps of peak flow were over-weighted.
Accumulate each value times the step length and divide by the reporting
time (routing_stats.report_time), or for an outfall by the new
NodeData::stat_outfall_time, the time it discharged. The pump average was
already volume / running time.

Requires: BND-19
Requires: BND-20

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after BND-19_swmm600.patch and BND-20_swmm600.patch:
    git apply CON-21_swmm600.patch

